---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { loadTimeline } from "../lib/timeline";

const { profile } = loadTimeline();
---

<Legal
  title="Terms"
  description={`Terms of use for ${profile.name}'s personal site.`}
  effective="2026-10-22"
>
  <p>
    These terms cover your use of ianpascoe.dev, {profile.name}'s personal site. By using the site you agree to them. If
    you don't, please don't use it.
  </p>

  <h2>What the site is</h2>
  <p>
    The site presents {profile.name.split(" ")[0]}'s career and work for information only. Nothing on it is an offer,
    a contract, professional advice, or a statement on behalf of any employer, client or organisation named on it.
    Views are {profile.name.split(" ")[0]}'s own.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    The record is kept carefully, but it is provided as is and may contain errors or fall out of date. Figures such as
    percentages, rankings and counts describe specific past work in the context given and are not guarantees of future
    results.
  </p>

  <h2>Ownership</h2>
  <p>
    The text, portrait, design and the rendering of the disk are © {profile.name}. You may link to any page, quote
    short passages with attribution, and print or save the resume for evaluating {profile.name.split(" ")[0]} for a role.
    Anything beyond that needs written permission.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site's source code is published for reference on <a
      href="https://github.com/ian-pascoe/ian-pascoe"
      rel="noopener">GitHub</a
    >. Publishing it does not grant a licence to reuse it unless a licence file in the repository says
    otherwise.
  </p>
  <p>
    Company names, product names and logos (for example RTX, AWS, GitHub and LinkedIn) belong to their owners. They
    appear only to identify where work was done or which tools were used, and do not imply endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Don't attempt to disrupt, overload or gain unauthorised access to the site or its hosting, and don't use its content
    to impersonate {profile.name.split(" ")[0]} or misrepresent his work.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to services run by others, such as GitHub, LinkedIn, X and project sites. Their content and terms
    are their own responsibility.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty and limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided as is and as available, without warranties of any kind, express or implied. To the fullest
    extent the law allows, {profile.name} is not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of the site or
    reliance on its content.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>What the site collects, and what it doesn't, is described in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Florida, United States, without regard to its conflict of law
    rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may be updated; the current version is always posted here with its effective date. Continuing to use
    the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms go to <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
